# Cross-platform line-ending policy (Issue #2760).
#
# GitHub Windows runners default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which checks out text
# files with CRLF. Several tests parse source as raw text and would see shifted
# byte offsets / spurious "\r" characters under CRLF:
#   - tests/pyi_stub_completeness.rs reads `fluxion.pyi` and `src/lib.rs`
#   - the PyO3 pytest suite imports pure-Python modules under tests/python/
#
# Pin LF for the file types the bindings test suite compiles, parses, or
# imports so behaviour is identical on ubuntu / windows / macos runners.
*.pyi   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.rs    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
